nodecode-followups is a rewrite of xiaok's xiaok/hermes-autonomous:

  https://github.com/xiaok/hermes-autonomous
  commit 431c5fa31eceb5341504ef71db5b4bdb8d493036
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 xiaok (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the board of follow-ups and the four origins a follow-up comes
from (care, utility, risk, curiosity); the gate that decides whether one may
go out now, with the same 23:00-08:00 quiet window, 90-minute cooldown,
muted categories, at most three items and at most six lines; the same
"looked at it" backoff and the same outcomes, with three ignored or one
annoyed muting a category for a while; the update-by-key rule; and the
review prompt's habits, kept as the manual on (help :followups) and the
primer the four tools are described by.

Left out, because Nodecode has no DM relay and no cron of its own here: the
Python helper's SQLite store and its `send` subcommand (the board is one
JSON file under the home, and the reminder reaches the model at its next
request instead of being pushed to a chat); the `/followups doctor` cron
repair pass; the wake gate that woke a scheduled agent only when something
was due; and the offline scene runner (`decide.py`) with its scenario
fixtures. Each of those belongs to the host's scheduler or its messaging
lane; the judgement they carried -- what is worth coming back to, and when --
is in the prompt and in the gate, and both are here.
